			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_570427327012460969">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791476057682', '591818032096020774', '570427327012457795', '110890513', '570427327012460969' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_570427327012460969">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c570427327012460432">fearthesloth</a></b>:</div><blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c570427327012459672">Cadence Squirrel</a></b>:</div>I would if I could. Best I could help with would be script writing. </blockquote>Why can't you volunteer? You're the one with an issue about a small dev team of just <b>two people</b> using AI to assist them, which I think is a bit rubbish of you. So if you have such a big issue about this, why can't you pitch in and help them with the translation? </blockquote>Being a small team is no excuse for being lazy and half-assing things like localisations which some people need to even play the game. If you actually put the effort into finding people you can find real talented translators who will volunteer or work cheaply, using AI is just lazy and is an insult to the people who genuinely need translations, we don't put up with ♥♥♥♥♥♥ dubs, why should we put up with lazy AI translations in a paid game?			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
