				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_568175573451409947">
				I agree, using AI for translation is really stupid. And for the AI stans out there, the actual problem with using AI translation is that it's less refined and uses far more physical resources than the computer-assisted translation tools we already have, and have used for decades. <br><br>AI translators have been systemically overpromising what they can deliver vs using traditional CAT with it's multiple decades worth of translation memories and glossaries and centuries of references. They are shoe-horning themselves into a field that they are not only not ready for, but actively stealing source reference from. That's it.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
									<div></div>
				
				
